    "whoWeAre": "WHO WE ARE",
    "whoWeAreDesc": "The Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA) is a government department which was responsible for the development, maintenance, and operation of the port of Colombo and other ports in Sri Lanka. The department was established in 1979 under the provisions of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority Act No. 15 of 1979. The Ports Authority does not receive financial allocations from the government but operates on its revenue. The SLPA is responsible for the maintenance of cargo handling equipment and infrastructure, pilotage, and shipping services. The government funded all stevedoring and handling operations until 1990 when private wharf companies were allowed to take over these activities. No. 31 of 1984 amended the Act to create two statutory corporations: the Sri Lanka Ports Authority and the Port of Colombo. The amended structure of the Ports Authority does not receive financial allocations from the government but operates on its revenue.",
